[2.498, "o", "### Findings\r\n\r\nThe session expiration is determined by the `ExpiresAt` field of the `Session` struct. The `Active` method checks if the current time is before the `ExpiresAt` time. The repository claims that `Put` and `Active` are safe for concurrent callers, but the implementation of `Store.sessions` (a map) lacks explicit synchronization mechanisms like locks or mutexes. Therefore, concurrent access to the session store is not safe.\r\n\r\n### Evidence\r\n\r\n*   **Session Expiration:** The `Session` struct in `session/store.go` contains an `ExpiresAt` field of type `time.Time`. The `Active` method in `session/store.go` checks if the provided `now` time is before `session.ExpiresAt`.\r\n*   **Concurrent Access:** The `Store` struct in `session/store.go` uses a `map[string]Session` named `sessions` to store session data. There are no mutexes, locks, or other synchronization primitives visible in the `Put` or `Active` methods to protect concurrent access to this map. The `TestStoreSupportsConcurrentAccess` function in"]
[0.000, "o", " `session/store_test.go` uses `sync.WaitGroup` and goroutines to exercise concurrent calls to `Put` and `Active`, but this test does not make the shared state safe.\r\n\r\n### Verification\r\n"]
